# Stories Super-Admin

## Routes

| Path | Component | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `/super-admin/stories` | `stories/page.tsx` | List with search, active toggle, sort |
| `/super-admin/stories/add` | `stories/add/page.tsx` | Create new story |
| `/super-admin/stories/[id]/edit` | `stories/[id]/edit/page.tsx` | Edit existing story |

## Role Guard

Every stories page guards access with `useCurrentUser`:

```tsx
const { user, isStoreManager } = useCurrentUser();
const isSuperAdmin = (user?.roleName ?? "").toLowerCase() === "superadmin";
const hasAccess = isSuperAdmin || isStoreManager;

useEffect(() => {
  if (user && !hasAccess) router.replace("/super-admin");
}, [user, hasAccess, router]);
```

Editors and Customers are redirected. Store Managers and Superadmins have full access.

## Sidebar Entry

In `apps/frontend/src/constants/superAdminSidebar.tsx`, the stories item is a **top-level SidebarItem** (not under blog):

```tsx
{
  id: "stories",
  label: "استوری‌ها",
  href: "/super-admin/stories",
  icon: <FiPlayCircle className="h-5 w-5 text-infinity-primary" stroke="#3d4c6e" />,
  children: [
    { id: "stories-list", label: "لیست استوری‌ها", href: "/super-admin/stories" },
    { id: "stories-add",  label: "افزودن استوری",   href: "/super-admin/stories/add" },
  ],
}
```

**Important:** `"stories"` is NOT in `STORE_MANAGER_HIDDEN_PARENT_IDS`, so store managers can see it. Do not add it there.

## StoryForm Component

`apps/frontend/src/components/Stories/StoryForm.tsx`

Shared between add and edit pages. Accepts:
- `initialValues?: Partial<StoryFormValues>` — pre-filled for edit
- `onSubmit: (data: CreateStoryData) => Promise<void>`
- `isLoading: boolean`
- `submitLabel: string`

**Fields exposed in the UI:**
- **Title** — required text input
- **Media** — single upload (image or video), required; type auto-detected from MIME
- **Cover image (Thumbnail)** — optional image shown on the avatar ring in the homepage rail
- **IsActive** — published / draft toggle
- **SortOrder** — integer, lower = shown first

Media upload uses `uploadFile` from `@/services/super-admin/files/upload`.

**Validation (client-side, Persian toast errors):**
1. Title required
2. Media required (must have uploaded `mediaId`)

## Media Upload Pattern

```typescript
import { uploadFile } from "@/services/super-admin/files/upload";

const result = await uploadFile(file);
if (result?.[0]) {
  setMediaId(result[0].id);   // Strapi media ID → send to API
  setMediaUrl(result[0].url); // Preview URL
}
```

The `id` (not the URL) is sent to the backend in `CreateStoryData.Media`.

## Image URL Construction

Media URLs from Strapi may be relative (e.g. `/uploads/image.webp`). Always prefix with `IMAGE_BASE_URL` if not absolute:

```typescript
const fullUrl = url.startsWith("http") ? url : `${IMAGE_BASE_URL}${url}`;
```
